## P1 — Image coverage (reconciled 2026-09-02)

- [x] Reconciled the existing cache by stable hero/skin identity only. Exactly
      798 unambiguous images are Pillow render-verified, SHA-256 verified, bound
      to both `skins.image_path` and the primary `skin_assets` row, and preferred
      by the detail UI. Coverage is 798 / 960 skins (83.13%) and 798 / 806 URL
      rows (99.01%). The default CLI remains dry-run; `--apply` creates a
      SQLite-consistent backup and updates one transaction.
- [ ] 154 / 960 skins have no image URL (URL coverage: 806 / 960, 83.96%).
- [ ] Six URL-backed rows have no matching cached image.
- [ ] Two duplicate `后羿 / 黄金射手座` database identities are ambiguous and
      deliberately remain unbound; this workflow does not deduplicate them.
- [x] URL coverage, verified local binding, renderability, unresolved reasons,
      conflict preservation, and second-run idempotence have separate measurable
      checks in `tests/test_image_reconciliation.py` and ignored JSON reports.

## P1 — Perceived-premium radar

- [x] Five-page dashboard embeds only the canonical
